  "description": "If you like all the advantages of what big wheels have to offer, but don’t like big wheeled bike geometry, the Beasley 650B series has your name written all over it. 650B wheels measure about 27.5”…which is halfway in between a 26” wheel and a 29” wheel. The main advantage of 650B wheels is that this “tweener” size can be used with 26” wheel frame geometry. The result is improved standover, better handling, and not being overwhelmed by that “big bike” feeling.",
